# S2: the AUDITED smoke of the publication traces (L1 of docs/tp4-traced-publish.md): c2-packed-tp4-gate-fcommit, the fused commit with in-place slides, the verify audits ON and
# QWEN_FAST_FUSED_COMMIT_AUDIT=1: before every fused launch today's eager publication runs and every delta and bank is compared bit for bit on every chip.
# Prerequisite: the one-card two-head in-place slide proof (tp4-fcommit-jobs F1a, F1b) is green; this job does not run it.
# Read: '[PINDIAG] fused commit engaged' (not 'refused'); '[PACKED-FUSED-AUDIT]' lines with mismatches=0 every round and checked=80; no today-path reason but ramp and parity;
# no 'discard after in-place slide'; in concurrent4_steady at least one round with all four users fused; the texts equal the production smoke's. STOP on any mismatch or refusal.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1 to 3 min, build 10 to 30 min, the smoke 30 to 60 min: 100 min at most.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-scope window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-scope and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3s is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3s
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-fcommit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,concurrent4_code_equal
